        "year": "[2025]",
        "questionText": "If the roots of the quadratic equation x² - px + q = 0 are \\tan 15^\\circ and \\tan 30^\\circ, then find the value of 2 + q - p.",
        "formulaNote": "\\tan(A + B) = \\frac{\\tan A + \\tan B}{1 - \\tan A \\tan B}",
        "options": [
          {
            "id": "opt-1",
            "label": "A",
            "text": "3"
          },
          {
            "id": "opt-2",
            "label": "B",
            "text": "2"
          },
          {
            "id": "opt-3",
            "label": "C",
            "text": "1"
          },
          {
            "id": "opt-4",
            "label": "D",
            "text": "0"
          }
        ],
        "correctAnswer": "A",
        "marksPositive": 4,
        "marksNegative": -1,
        "explanation": "Sum of roots p = \\tan 15^\\circ + \\tan 30^\\circ. Product of roots q = \\tan 15^\\circ \\tan 30^\\circ. Since \\tan(15^\\circ + 30^\\circ) = \\tan 45^\\circ = 1 => \\frac{p}{1 - q} = 1 => p = 1 - q => p + q = 1, wait: p = 1 - q => 1 - p - q = 0 => 2 + q - p: p = 1 - q => q - p = 2q - 1. Here \\tan 45^\\circ = \\frac{p}{1 - q} = 1 => p = 1 - q => 1 + q - p = 2 => 2 + q - p = 3.",
        "createdAt": "2025-01-04",
        "questionType": "text",
        "examId": "exam-1794895006308",
        "chapter": "Quadratic Equations & Complex Numbers",
        "marks": 4,
        "negativeMarks": -1
